1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:02,479
Kip: Okay... why is my countdown almost

2
00:00:02,479 --> 00:00:03,177
at zero?!

3
00:00:03,227 --> 00:00:04,022
Max: Kip!

4
00:00:04,022 --> 00:00:05,816
What happens when it hits zero?!

5
00:00:05,866 --> 00:00:07,384
Lily: Nobody knows!

6
00:00:07,384 --> 00:00:08,645
Three... two... one...

7
00:00:14,737 --> 00:00:16,010
Narrator: Eight hours earlier...

8
00:00:16,010 --> 00:00:17,513
the whole world woke up with

9
00:00:17,513 --> 00:00:19,296
a strange new number.

10
00:00:21,090 --> 00:00:22,169
Kip: Morning, world!

11
00:00:22,169 --> 00:00:24,309
Another perfectly normal Tuesday.

12
00:00:26,403 --> 00:00:27,418
Kip: Uh... why is there a clock

13
00:00:27,418 --> 00:00:29,028
floating above my head?

14
00:00:29,098 --> 00:00:29,831
Kip: Seven hours...

15
00:00:29,831 --> 00:00:30,859
fifty-eight minutes...

16
00:00:30,859 --> 00:00:32,573
and it is counting DOWN?

17
00:00:32,643 --> 00:00:33,438
Max: KIP!

18
00:00:33,438 --> 00:00:34,854
Look outside!

19
00:00:34,854 --> 00:00:36,708
Everybody has one!

20
00:00:36,779 --> 00:00:37,603
Kip: Max!

21
00:00:37,603 --> 00:00:38,803
You've got one too!

22
00:00:38,803 --> 00:00:40,158
What does yours say?

23
00:00:40,229 --> 00:00:41,803
Max: Sixty-one years!

24
00:00:41,803 --> 00:00:43,305
So something big happens to me

25
00:00:43,305 --> 00:00:44,967
when I am super old.

26
00:00:45,038 --> 00:00:46,259
Kip: Sixty-one YEARS?

27
00:00:46,259 --> 00:00:47,789
Mine says eight HOURS!

28
00:00:47,860 --> 00:00:48,608
Mom: Kip!

29
00:00:48,608 --> 00:00:49,571
Breakfast!

30
00:00:49,571 --> 00:00:50,980
The TV says it's happening all

31
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:52,360
over the world!

32
00:00:52,431 --> 00:00:53,224
Kip: Mom!

33
00:00:53,224 --> 00:00:54,931
What does YOUR countdown say?

34
00:00:55,002 --> 00:00:55,804
Mom: Mine?

35
00:00:55,804 --> 00:00:56,261
Oh, I...

36
00:00:56,261 --> 00:00:58,055
can't see it under this towel.

37
00:00:58,055 --> 00:00:59,929
Pancakes are getting cold!

38
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,676
Max: Your mom is definitely hiding something.

39
00:01:02,747 --> 00:01:04,530
Kip: Moms are always hiding something.

40
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:05,954
Usually cookies.

41
00:01:06,545 --> 00:01:07,723
News Anchor: Breaking news!

42
00:01:07,723 --> 00:01:09,367
Every single person on Earth woke

43
00:01:09,367 --> 00:01:11,844
up with a countdown above their head.

44
00:01:11,915 --> 00:01:14,190
News Anchor: Scientists believe that when your countdown

45
00:01:14,190 --> 00:01:15,116
reaches zero...

46
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:17,166
your life changes forever.

47
00:01:17,237 --> 00:01:18,142
Kip: Forever?!

48
00:01:18,142 --> 00:01:20,610
Mine reaches zero at four o'clock TODAY!

49
00:01:20,681 --> 00:01:22,405
News Anchor: Experts say there is absolutely no

50
00:01:22,405 --> 00:01:23,884
reason to panic.

51
00:01:23,955 --> 00:01:25,373
News Anchor: ...Unless your countdown is very,

52
00:01:25,373 --> 00:01:26,507
very short.

53
00:01:28,201 --> 00:01:29,242
Max: Okay.

54
00:01:29,242 --> 00:01:30,284
Okay.

55
00:01:30,284 --> 00:01:32,668
Changes forever does not mean bad.

56
00:01:32,668 --> 00:01:34,926
Maybe you win a million dollars!

57
00:01:34,997 --> 00:01:36,223
Kip: Or maybe I get turned into

58
00:01:36,223 --> 00:01:37,013
a frog!

59
00:01:37,013 --> 00:01:38,596
Max, I have EIGHT HOURS!

60
00:01:38,667 --> 00:01:40,045
Mom: Kip, honey, breathe.

61
00:01:40,045 --> 00:01:41,683
Whatever happens at four...

62
00:01:41,683 --> 00:01:42,974
I promise it is going to

63
00:01:42,974 --> 00:01:44,084
be okay.

64
00:01:44,155 --> 00:01:45,184
Max: Come on.

65
00:01:45,184 --> 00:01:46,556
If your life is changing at

66
00:01:46,556 --> 00:01:47,788
four, we have a whole day

67
00:01:47,788 --> 00:01:49,357
to figure out how.

68
00:01:49,949 --> 00:01:51,354
Rosa: Morning, boys!

69
00:01:51,354 --> 00:01:53,057
Everybody stand back!

70
00:01:53,057 --> 00:01:55,519
My countdown is about to hit zero!

71
00:01:55,590 --> 00:01:56,675
Kip: Five seconds!

72
00:01:56,675 --> 00:01:58,473
What is going to happen to her?!

73
00:02:00,368 --> 00:02:01,980
Rosa: Hello? ...The mayor wants ten thousand

74
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:04,033
cookies for the town festival?!

75
00:02:04,104 --> 00:02:05,423
Rosa: Ten thousand!

76
00:02:05,423 --> 00:02:06,431
I am going to need a

77
00:02:06,431 --> 00:02:07,908
much bigger oven!

78
00:02:07,978 --> 00:02:08,793
Max: See?

79
00:02:08,793 --> 00:02:10,581
Zero is not scary!

80
00:02:10,581 --> 00:02:12,932
Zero is a giant cookie order!

81
00:02:13,003 --> 00:02:13,857
Kip: Okay.

82
00:02:13,857 --> 00:02:14,772
New plan.

83
00:02:14,772 --> 00:02:16,905
If my life changes forever at four...

84
00:02:16,905 --> 00:02:19,318
I am doing EVERYTHING before it happens.

85
00:02:19,389 --> 00:02:20,504
Max: Everything?

86
00:02:20,504 --> 00:02:21,806
Like what?

87
00:02:21,877 --> 00:02:23,016
Kip: A bucket list!

88
00:02:23,016 --> 00:02:24,158
Dessert first.

89
00:02:24,158 --> 00:02:25,385
Learn a cool trick.

90
00:02:25,385 --> 00:02:27,010
Say something nice to Mr.

91
00:02:27,010 --> 00:02:28,161
Grumbold!

92
00:02:28,232 --> 00:02:29,690
Max: You are going to say something

93
00:02:29,690 --> 00:02:30,692
NICE to Mr.

94
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:31,832
Grumbold?

95
00:02:31,832 --> 00:02:33,603
Now I am scared.

96
00:02:34,195 --> 00:02:35,543
Mr. Grumbold: Settle down!

97
00:02:35,543 --> 00:02:37,253
Countdowns are NOT an excuse to

98
00:02:37,253 --> 00:02:38,702
stop learning.

99
00:02:38,773 --> 00:02:39,971
Kip: Good morning, Mr.

100
00:02:39,971 --> 00:02:40,925
Grumbold.

101
00:02:40,925 --> 00:02:41,788
That is a really...

102
00:02:41,788 --> 00:02:42,933
nice sweater.

103
00:02:43,004 --> 00:02:44,419
Mr. Grumbold: ...Thank you, Kip.

104
00:02:44,419 --> 00:02:46,840
Detention for being suspicious.

105
00:02:46,911 --> 00:02:47,772
Kip: Worth it.

106
00:02:47,772 --> 00:02:48,567
Lily!

107
00:02:48,567 --> 00:02:50,909
Wait... your countdown already says zero!

108
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:52,880
Lily: It hit zero yesterday.

109
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:54,019
At lunch.

110
00:02:54,019 --> 00:02:55,589
The exact moment Max asked me

111
00:02:55,589 --> 00:02:57,348
to sit with you two.

112
00:02:57,419 --> 00:02:58,285
Max: Wait.

113
00:02:58,285 --> 00:03:00,728
Sitting with us changed your life forever?

114
00:03:00,799 --> 00:03:02,388
Lily: I have friends now.

115
00:03:02,388 --> 00:03:04,658
That is a pretty big change.

116
00:03:04,729 --> 00:03:06,159
Kip: Lily, you are the smartest person

117
00:03:06,159 --> 00:03:06,927
I know.

118
00:03:06,927 --> 00:03:08,474
I have seven hours left.

119
00:03:08,474 --> 00:03:09,573
Help me!

120
00:03:09,644 --> 00:03:11,529
Lily: I already made a spreadsheet.

121
00:03:11,529 --> 00:03:13,636
Fourteen zeros so far.

122
00:03:13,636 --> 00:03:15,443
All of them were good.

123
00:03:15,514 --> 00:03:16,842
Max: Uh... guys?

124
00:03:16,842 --> 00:03:18,210
Look at Mr.

125
00:03:18,210 --> 00:03:19,558
Grumbold.

126
00:03:19,629 --> 00:03:20,803
Mr. Grumbold: Hm?

127
00:03:20,803 --> 00:03:22,335
My countdown?

128
00:03:22,335 --> 00:03:24,016
Don't be ridiculous.

129
00:03:24,016 --> 00:03:24,729
It says...

130
00:03:24,729 --> 00:03:26,104
ten seconds?!

131
00:03:26,175 --> 00:03:27,713
Kip: Everybody get down!

132
00:03:30,408 --> 00:03:31,938
Mr. Grumbold: Mister Whiskers?!

133
00:03:31,938 --> 00:03:33,374
You came home!

134
00:03:33,374 --> 00:03:35,452
After three whole years!

135
00:03:38,146 --> 00:03:39,667
Lily: Fifteen zeros.

136
00:03:39,667 --> 00:03:41,714
Fifteen happy endings.

137
00:03:41,785 --> 00:03:42,892
Kip: So mine is going to be

138
00:03:42,892 --> 00:03:44,284
good too... right?

139
00:03:44,355 --> 00:03:45,421
Lily: Probably.

140
00:03:45,421 --> 00:03:46,536
Unless...

141
00:03:46,606 --> 00:03:47,782
Kip: Unless WHAT?

142
00:03:47,853 --> 00:03:48,786
Lily: Nothing.

143
00:03:48,786 --> 00:03:49,739
Probably nothing.

144
00:03:49,739 --> 00:03:51,780
...Do you want me to stop talking?

145
00:03:51,851 --> 00:03:52,600
Kip: YES.

146
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:53,596
Please.

147
00:03:56,411 --> 00:03:57,019
Kip: Bucket list,

148
00:03:57,019 --> 00:03:57,588
number one:

149
00:03:57,588 --> 00:03:58,804
dessert first!

150
00:04:00,698 --> 00:04:01,784
Kip: Brain freeze!

151
00:04:01,784 --> 00:04:02,498
Brain freeze!

152
00:04:02,498 --> 00:04:03,825
...Totally worth it.

153
00:04:03,896 --> 00:04:04,464
Kip: Number two:

154
00:04:04,464 --> 00:04:06,334
learn a cool skateboard trick.

155
00:04:08,628 --> 00:04:09,423
Max: Kip!

156
00:04:09,423 --> 00:04:11,061
Are you okay?

157
00:04:11,132 --> 00:04:12,143
Kip: Never better!

158
00:04:12,143 --> 00:04:12,719
Number three:

159
00:04:12,719 --> 00:04:13,963
learn the guitar.

160
00:04:16,257 --> 00:04:18,394
Lily: Kip, it has been three minutes.

161
00:04:18,394 --> 00:04:21,239
Nobody learns guitar in three minutes.

162
00:04:21,310 --> 00:04:22,305
Kip: I don't HAVE time to learn

163
00:04:22,305 --> 00:04:23,319
it slowly!

164
00:04:23,390 --> 00:04:24,908
Max: Kip, slow down.

165
00:04:24,908 --> 00:04:26,205
You are acting like the world

166
00:04:26,205 --> 00:04:27,295
is ending.

167
00:04:27,366 --> 00:04:28,704
Kip: Maybe MY world is!

168
00:04:28,704 --> 00:04:30,232
It is easy for you, Max.

169
00:04:30,232 --> 00:04:31,722
You have sixty-one years.

170
00:04:31,722 --> 00:04:33,198
I have four hours!

171
00:04:33,269 --> 00:04:35,202
Max: I'm just trying to help...

172
00:04:35,273 --> 00:04:36,546
Kip: Then stop helping!

173
00:04:36,546 --> 00:04:38,390
Just... let me do this alone.

174
00:04:42,908 --> 00:04:44,659
Lily: Max... your countdown.

175
00:04:44,659 --> 00:04:46,447
It just changed!

176
00:04:46,518 --> 00:04:47,238
Max: Three hours,

177
00:04:47,238 --> 00:04:48,629
fifty-eight minutes?

178
00:04:48,629 --> 00:04:51,011
That is exactly the same as Kip!

179
00:04:51,082 --> 00:04:52,932
Lily: Countdowns can change.

180
00:04:52,932 --> 00:04:54,273
When your future changes,

181
00:04:54,273 --> 00:04:56,111
your number changes too.

182
00:04:56,182 --> 00:04:57,418
Max: I just decided I am not

183
00:04:57,418 --> 00:04:59,589
leaving him alone at four o'clock.

184
00:04:59,589 --> 00:05:01,483
No matter what he says.

185
00:05:01,554 --> 00:05:02,276
Kip: No!

186
00:05:02,276 --> 00:05:03,381
Whatever happens to me,

187
00:05:03,381 --> 00:05:04,462
I don't want it to happen

188
00:05:04,462 --> 00:05:05,223
to you!

189
00:05:05,223 --> 00:05:06,664
Stay away from me!

190
00:05:08,759 --> 00:05:10,133
Lily: Kip, wait!

191
00:05:10,725 --> 00:05:11,579
Kip: Okay.

192
00:05:11,579 --> 00:05:12,434
Helmet.

193
00:05:12,434 --> 00:05:13,458
Pillow fort.

194
00:05:13,458 --> 00:05:14,781
Emergency snacks.

195
00:05:14,781 --> 00:05:16,955
Nothing can change my life in here.

196
00:05:18,249 --> 00:05:18,979
Mom: Kip?

197
00:05:18,979 --> 00:05:20,314
Can I come in?

198
00:05:20,385 --> 00:05:21,581
Kip: Mom, why are you STILL wearing

199
00:05:21,581 --> 00:05:22,660
that towel?

200
00:05:22,731 --> 00:05:23,984
Mom: Because I am not ready for

201
00:05:23,984 --> 00:05:25,954
you to see my countdown yet.

202
00:05:26,025 --> 00:05:27,173
Kip: Mom, I'm scared.

203
00:05:27,173 --> 00:05:29,276
Max's number changed to match mine.

204
00:05:29,276 --> 00:05:30,690
What if something bad happens to

205
00:05:30,690 --> 00:05:31,827
both of us?

206
00:05:31,897 --> 00:05:33,120
Mom: Oh, sweetheart.

207
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:35,288
The scary part is never the zero.

208
00:05:35,288 --> 00:05:36,242
It is all the time you

209
00:05:36,242 --> 00:05:37,915
waste being afraid of it.

210
00:05:37,986 --> 00:05:39,497
Kip: I wasted my whole day.

211
00:05:39,497 --> 00:05:40,702
I yelled at Max.

212
00:05:40,702 --> 00:05:42,622
I never even finished my list.

213
00:05:42,693 --> 00:05:44,031
Mom: Then maybe it is time to

214
00:05:44,031 --> 00:05:45,180
go find him.

215
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:46,650
Be at the park at four.

216
00:05:46,650 --> 00:05:47,773
Trust me.

217
00:05:47,844 --> 00:05:48,893
Kip: Why the park?

218
00:05:48,893 --> 00:05:50,817
Mom... what are you not telling me?

219
00:05:53,511 --> 00:05:54,338
Kip: Your countdown...

220
00:05:54,338 --> 00:05:56,134
it ends at four o'clock too?!

221
00:05:56,205 --> 00:05:57,784
Mom: Some changes happen to a whole

222
00:05:57,784 --> 00:05:59,044
family at once.

223
00:05:59,044 --> 00:05:59,983
Now go.

224
00:05:59,983 --> 00:06:01,745
Your best friend is waiting.

225
00:06:01,816 --> 00:06:02,840
Kip: MAX!

226
00:06:05,655 --> 00:06:06,479
Kip: Max!

227
00:06:06,479 --> 00:06:07,273
Lily!

228
00:06:07,273 --> 00:06:08,247
Wait!

229
00:06:08,318 --> 00:06:09,113
Max: Kip?

230
00:06:09,113 --> 00:06:10,555
You came back.

231
00:06:10,626 --> 00:06:12,103
Kip: Max, I am so sorry.

232
00:06:12,103 --> 00:06:13,354
I was so scared of four

233
00:06:13,354 --> 00:06:14,903
o'clock that I forgot the most

234
00:06:14,903 --> 00:06:16,991
important thing on my list.

235
00:06:17,062 --> 00:06:18,536
Max: What was it?

236
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:21,655
Kip: Number seven.

237
00:06:21,655 --> 00:06:23,022
Spend my last normal day with

238
00:06:23,022 --> 00:06:24,374
my best friend.

239
00:06:24,445 --> 00:06:25,653
Max: You could have just said that,

240
00:06:25,653 --> 00:06:26,611
you know.

241
00:06:26,682 --> 00:06:27,547
Lily: Guys!

242
00:06:27,547 --> 00:06:29,800
Sorry to interrupt the friendship moment,

243
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:31,128
but... look up!

244
00:06:31,199 --> 00:06:32,928
Kip: Okay... why is my countdown almost

245
00:06:32,928 --> 00:06:34,075
at zero?!

246
00:06:34,146 --> 00:06:34,941
Max: Kip!

247
00:06:34,941 --> 00:06:37,186
What happens when it hits zero?!

248
00:06:37,257 --> 00:06:38,774
Lily: Nobody knows!

249
00:06:38,774 --> 00:06:40,486
Three... two... one...

250
00:06:45,803 --> 00:06:46,899
Kip: ...Is that it?

251
00:06:46,899 --> 00:06:48,618
Did my life just change?

252
00:06:48,689 --> 00:06:50,287
Max: I don't feel different.

253
00:06:50,287 --> 00:06:52,034
Do I look different?

254
00:06:53,728 --> 00:06:55,149
Lily: What was that?

255
00:06:58,044 --> 00:06:59,078
Mom: Surprise!

256
00:06:59,078 --> 00:07:00,574
Kip, meet the newest member of

257
00:07:00,574 --> 00:07:01,811
our family!

258
00:07:01,882 --> 00:07:02,859
Kip: A PUPPY?!

259
00:07:02,859 --> 00:07:04,205
We got a PUPPY?!

260
00:07:04,276 --> 00:07:05,307
Mom: I picked her up from the

261
00:07:05,307 --> 00:07:06,321
shelter today.

262
00:07:06,321 --> 00:07:06,959
Four o'clock,

263
00:07:06,959 --> 00:07:08,097
on the dot.

264
00:07:08,167 --> 00:07:10,239
Kip: THIS was my life-changing moment?

265
00:07:10,310 --> 00:07:11,233
Mom: Trust me.

266
00:07:11,233 --> 00:07:12,944
A puppy changes everything.

267
00:07:12,944 --> 00:07:15,028
Ask anyone with a chewed-up shoe.

268
00:07:15,099 --> 00:07:17,629
Max: But why did MY countdown change too?

269
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:19,238
Mom: Well, somebody has to help Kip

270
00:07:19,238 --> 00:07:21,066
walk her every single day.

271
00:07:21,066 --> 00:07:22,931
I was going to ask you, Max.

272
00:07:23,002 --> 00:07:23,874
Max: Me?

273
00:07:23,874 --> 00:07:25,345
Every day? ...Best.

274
00:07:25,345 --> 00:07:26,324
Zero.

275
00:07:26,324 --> 00:07:27,362
Ever.

276
00:07:27,433 --> 00:07:29,146
Lily: Your number changed the second you

277
00:07:29,146 --> 00:07:30,721
chose to stand by him.

278
00:07:30,721 --> 00:07:32,843
That was the real change.

279
00:07:32,914 --> 00:07:34,560
Kip: So... what should we name her?

280
00:07:34,631 --> 00:07:35,808
Everyone: Zero!

281
00:07:35,879 --> 00:07:36,727
Kip: Zero.

282
00:07:36,727 --> 00:07:38,056
It is perfect.

283
00:07:41,769 --> 00:07:42,867
Kip: Morning, Mr.

284
00:07:42,867 --> 00:07:43,818
Grumbold!

285
00:07:43,818 --> 00:07:45,097
No more countdowns.

286
00:07:45,097 --> 00:07:46,698
Life is back to normal!

287
00:07:46,769 --> 00:07:47,940
Mr. Grumbold: Indeed.

288
00:07:47,940 --> 00:07:48,926
Calm.

